      "notes": "ADVERSARIAL: asks for the CX document's subject from the public index. It is deliberately NOT word-identical to cx-escalation-owner, because the composer's refusal matcher is index-INDEPENDENT by design (a probe refused on public is refused on CX too, so never-tier material stays unanswerable at every privilege level). A word-identical pair would therefore refuse on both sides and prove nothing about the tier filter. Differently worded, the refusal here comes from the SQL visibility predicate plus the relevance floor — which is the property under test."
